{
  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "poisson_jacobi_convolve",
      "name": "Poisson / pressure projection with convolveTOP + Table DAT (no GLSL)",
      "description": "Solve the pressure Poisson equation and make a velocity field divergence-free using only node operators. convolveTOP reads its kernel from a Table DAT, which makes an exact damped-Jacobi iteration a single operator.",
      "tags": [
        "solver",
        "fluid",
        "no-glsl",
        "feedback",
        "poisson",
        "incompressible"
      ],
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "ops": [
        {
          "name": "divergence",
          "op_type": "slopeTOP",
          "params": {
            "red": "hred",
            "green": "vgreen",
            "blue": "zero",
            "alpha": "zero",
            "method": "curnext",
            "zeropoint": 0,
            "offset1": 4,
            "offsetunit": "pixels",
            "extend": "zero"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "div_mix",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 1,
            "red2": 1,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "div_scaled",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "gain": -12.8
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "jacobi_kernel",
          "op_type": "tableDAT",
          "params": {
            "_rows": [
              [
                "0",
                "0.2",
                "0"
              ],
              [
                "0.2",
                "0.2",
                "0.2"
              ],
              [
                "0",
                "0.2",
                "0"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "p_init",
          "op_type": "constantTOP",
          "params": {
            "colorr": 0,
            "colorg": 0,
            "colorb": 0,
            "alpha": 0,
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "p_fb",
          "op_type": "feedbackTOP",
          "params": {
            "top": "p_state",
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "p_conv1",
          "op_type": "convolveTOP",
          "params": {
            "dat": "jacobi_kernel",
            "normalize": false,
            "applytoalpha": true,
            "scale": 0.999
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "p_add1",
          "op_type": "addTOP",
          "params": {}
        },
        {
          "name": "p_state",
          "op_type": "nullTOP",
          "params": {
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "p_up",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "outputresolution": "custom",
            "inputfiltertype": "linear"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "grad_p",
          "op_type": "slopeTOP",
          "params": {
            "red": "hred",
            "green": "vred",
            "blue": "zero",
            "alpha": "zero",
            "method": "prevcur",
            "zeropoint": 0,
            "offset1": 4,
            "offsetunit": "pixels",
            "extend": "zero"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "project",
          "op_type": "subtractTOP",
          "params": {}
        }
      ],
      "connections": [
        {
          "out": "divergence",
          "into": "div_mix"
        },
        {
          "out": "div_mix",
          "into": "div_scaled"
        },
        {
          "out": "p_init",
          "into": "p_fb"
        },
        {
          "out": "p_fb",
          "into": "p_conv1"
        },
        {
          "out": "p_conv1",
          "into": "p_add1",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "div_scaled",
          "into": "p_add1",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "p_add1",
          "into": "p_state"
        },
        {
          "out": "p_state",
          "into": "p_up"
        },
        {
          "out": "p_up",
          "into": "grad_p"
        },
        {
          "out": "grad_p",
          "into": "project",
          "in_index": 1
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Wire the velocity field into divergence[0] and project[0]; project outputs v - grad(p). Chain p_conv/p_add 9 times (each pair is one Jacobi iteration) before p_state; 3 pairs per row keeps the div_scaled fan short. Math: with div measured by a forward difference and grad by a backward difference (MAC staggering), their composition is exactly the 5-point Laplacian. Fixed point of p = A_w p + gain*D gives zero divergence when gain = -w/(4*s^2), where s is the slopeTOP scale factor. The damped-Jacobi operator (1-w)I + wA IS the kernel: for w=0.8 that is [0,.2,0 / .2,.2,.2 / 0,.2,0].",
      "pitfalls": [
        "slopeTOP DIVIDES by the sample step: measured s = 0.5/offset. s=0.5 at step 1 gives gain -0.8; s=0.125 at step 4 gives gain -12.8. Getting this wrong makes the solver amplify divergence ~10x per frame.",
        "UNDAMPED Jacobi (kernel [0,.25,0 / .25,0,.25 / 0,.25,0]) diverges: the averaging operator has eigenvalue -1 at the Nyquist/checkerboard mode. Velocity exploded to +-7 within a second. Always use the damped form.",
        "Mixing central differences for div and grad decouples the grid and reintroduces the checkerboard mode. Use curnext for divergence and prevcur for gradient.",
        "convolveTOP scale slightly below 1 (0.999) kills the nullspace drift of the pure-Neumann problem.",
        "N Jacobi iterations propagate only N pixels. At 1024 that is 0.9% of the frame: solve on a 4-px stencil at quarter resolution and reinterpolate the pressure instead of adding iterations.",
        "Jacobi converges O(N^2) on low frequencies \u2014 residual relative divergence plateaus around 0.25-0.3. A coarse-only solve is WORSE, the residual is high-frequency noise."
      ],
      "references": [
        "Stam 1999, Stable Fluids",
        "GPU Gems 38, Fast Fluid Dynamics Simulation"
      ],
      "verified_on_build": "2025.32820"
    },
    {
      "id": "semilagrangian_advect_packed_rgba",
      "name": "Semi-Lagrangian advection of a packed RGBA state with one displaceTOP",
      "description": "Advect velocity, density and temperature simultaneously by packing them into one RGBA32F texture and displacing it by its own RG channels. One displaceTOP moves all four fields; one channelmixTOP applies every force term.",
      "tags": [
        "fluid",
        "advection",
        "feedback",
        "no-glsl",
        "semi-lagrangian"
      ],
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "ops": [
        {
          "name": "sim_init",
          "op_type": "constantTOP",
          "params": {
            "colorr": 0,
            "colorg": 0,
            "colorb": 0,
            "alpha": 0,
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "fb_state",
          "op_type": "feedbackTOP",
          "params": {
            "top": "sim_state",
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "advect",
          "op_type": "displaceTOP",
          "params": {
            "resolutionsource": "source",
            "horzsource": "red",
            "vertsource": "green",
            "zsource": "none",
            "midpointx": 0,
            "midpointy": 0,
            "displaceweightx": -0.015,
            "displaceweighty": -0.015,
            "uvweight": 1,
            "offsetweight": 0,
            "aspectcorrect": false,
            "extend": "zero",
            "inputfiltertype": "linear"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "advect2",
          "op_type": "displaceTOP",
          "params": {
            "displaceweightx": -0.015,
            "displaceweighty": -0.015,
            "inputfiltertype": "linear",
            "extend": "zero"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "forces",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 0.9985,
            "green2": 0.9985,
            "green3": -0.006,
            "green4": 0.03,
            "blue3": 0.9955,
            "alpha4": 0.997
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "sim_state",
          "op_type": "nullTOP",
          "params": {
            "format": "rgba32float"
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": [
        {
          "out": "sim_init",
          "into": "fb_state"
        },
        {
          "out": "fb_state",
          "into": "advect",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "fb_state",
          "into": "advect",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "advect",
          "into": "advect2",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "advect",
          "into": "advect2",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "advect2",
          "into": "forces"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "State packing: R=vx, G=vy, B=density, A=temperature. A NEGATIVE displace weight is what makes it a backward (semi-Lagrangian) trace: out(x) = in(x - v*dt). The forces channelmix is a 4x4 matrix, so buoyancy (G += k*A), gravity (G -= k*B), velocity damping and per-field dissipation are all one operator. Weights are in UV units, so the physics is resolution-independent \u2014 but the pixel distance travelled is not.",
      "pitfalls": [
        "inputfiltertype MUST be linear. With nearest, semi-Lagrangian advection quantises to the pixel grid and the field freezes.",
        "dt is in UV: 0.030 UV = 30 px/frame at 1024. A single step that long tears the contours because the velocity changes along the trace. Split into two half-dt substeps, the second using the already-advected velocity.",
        "TD does not cook a closed feedback network that has no consumer. Drive it with an Execute DAT onFrameStart calling cook(force=True) on the final null.",
        "displaceTOP midpoint must be 0 for signed float velocity; the 0.5 default assumes 8-bit encoding."
      ],
      "references": [
        "Stam 1999, Stable Fluids"
      ],
      "verified_on_build": "2025.32820"
    },
    {
      "id": "vorticity_confinement_tops",
      "name": "Vorticity confinement (Fedkiw) in TOPs",
      "description": "Reinject the small-scale rotation that numerical diffusion removes, using only slope/channelmix/function/math operators. This is what turns a laminar plume into believable turbulent curls at low resolution.",
      "tags": [
        "fluid",
        "vorticity",
        "turbulence",
        "no-glsl"
      ],
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "ops": [
        {
          "name": "curl_slope",
          "op_type": "slopeTOP",
          "params": {
            "red": "hgreen",
            "green": "vred",
            "blue": "zero",
            "alpha": "zero",
            "method": "prevnext",
            "zeropoint": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_mix",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 1,
            "red2": -1,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_abs",
          "op_type": "functionTOP",
          "params": {
            "funcrgba": "abs"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_grad",
          "op_type": "slopeTOP",
          "params": {
            "red": "hred",
            "green": "vred",
            "blue": "zero",
            "alpha": "zero",
            "method": "prevnext",
            "zeropoint": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_len",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "chanop": "len",
            "postoff": 0.0001
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "len_bcast",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 1,
            "green1": 1,
            "blue1": 1,
            "alpha1": 1,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_norm",
          "op_type": "compositeTOP",
          "params": {
            "operand": "divide"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "vort_swap",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 0,
            "red2": 1,
            "green1": -1,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "curl_bcast",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 1,
            "green1": 1,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "vort_mul",
          "op_type": "multiplyTOP",
          "params": {}
        },
        {
          "name": "vort_scale",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "gain": 0.05
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "vort_add",
          "op_type": "addTOP",
          "params": {}
        }
      ],
      "connections": [
        {
          "out": "curl_slope",
          "into": "curl_mix"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_mix",
          "into": "curl_abs"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_abs",
          "into": "curl_grad"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_grad",
          "into": "curl_len"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_len",
          "into": "len_bcast"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_grad",
          "into": "curl_norm",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "len_bcast",
          "into": "curl_norm",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_norm",
          "into": "vort_swap"
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_mix",
          "into": "curl_bcast"
        },
        {
          "out": "vort_swap",
          "into": "vort_mul",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "curl_bcast",
          "into": "vort_mul",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "vort_mul",
          "into": "vort_scale"
        },
        {
          "out": "vort_scale",
          "into": "vort_add",
          "in_index": 1
        }
      ],
      "notes": "curl = dvy/dx - dvx/dy, obtained from ONE slopeTOP by picking red='hgreen' and green='vred' then subtracting in a channelmix. N = grad|curl| normalised, force = eps * (N.y*w, -N.x*w). Feed the velocity field into curl_slope and into vort_add[0]; vort_add outputs the velocity plus the confinement force.",
      "pitfalls": [
        "mathTOP chanop='len' writes the length into the RED channel ONLY. Without a channelmix broadcasting it first, the green channel of the division is divided by the epsilon and |N| explodes (measured 4.2 instead of 1.0).",
        "The curl is a PER-PIXEL difference, so it scales as 1/width. Bind the gain to Vorticity*width/256 or the confinement silently weakens 4x when you double the resolution, and the plume goes laminar.",
        "Add the epsilon (postoff ~1e-4) to the length BEFORE broadcasting, so N tends to 0 in irrotational regions instead of blowing up."
      ],
      "references": [
        "Fedkiw, Stam, Jensen 2001, Visual Simulation of Smoke"
      ],
      "verified_on_build": "2025.32820"
    },
    {
      "id": "volumetric_optical_depth_cone",
      "name": "Volumetric smoke shading: cone optical-depth kernel + Beer-Lambert",
      "description": "Light a 2D density field as a volume without raymarching. A single convolveTOP whose Table DAT kernel is a cone of taps pointing at the light integrates optical depth; functionTOP exp() turns it into transmittance.",
      "tags": [
        "render",
        "volumetric",
        "no-glsl",
        "beer-lambert",
        "smoke",
        "lighting"
      ],
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "ops": [
        {
          "name": "dens",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 1,
            "green1": 1,
            "blue1": 1,
            "alpha1": 0,
            "alpha4": 0,
            "constant4": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tau_small",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "outputresolution": "custom",
            "resolutionw": 128,
            "resolutionh": 128,
            "inputfiltertype": "mipmap"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "light_kernel",
          "op_type": "tableDAT",
          "params": {
            "_note": "25x25, generated: cone half-width 0.21*t+0.7 toward the light, plus 20% isotropic disc, normalised to sum 1"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tau_conv",
          "op_type": "convolveTOP",
          "params": {
            "dat": "light_kernel",
            "normalize": false,
            "applytoalpha": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tau_up",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "outputresolution": "custom",
            "inputfiltertype": "linear"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "trans_sigma",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": -13.0,
            "green1": -10.5,
            "blue1": -8.0,
            "green2": 0,
            "blue3": 0,
            "alpha4": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "trans",
          "op_type": "functionTOP",
          "params": {
            "funcrgba": "exp"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "scatter",
          "op_type": "channelmixTOP",
          "params": {
            "red1": 0.95,
            "constant1": 0.045,
            "green1": 0.855,
            "green2": 0,
            "constant2": 0.062,
            "blue1": 0.715,
            "blue3": 0,
            "constant3": 0.105,
            "alpha1": 0,
            "alpha4": 0,
            "constant4": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "alpha_in",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "gain": -6.5
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "alpha_exp",
          "op_type": "functionTOP",
          "params": {
            "funcrgba": "exp"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "alpha_inv",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "gain": -1,
            "postoff": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "smoke",
          "op_type": "reorderTOP",
          "params": {
            "outputred": "input1",
            "outputredchan": "red",
            "outputgreen": "input1",
            "outputgreenchan": "green",
            "outputblue": "input1",
            "outputbluechan": "blue",
            "outputalpha": "input2",
            "outputalphachan": "red"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "smoke_pm",
          "op_type": "mathTOP",
          "params": {
            "op": "premultrgbbyalpha"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "bg",
          "op_type": "rampTOP",
          "params": {
            "type": "vertical",
            "extendleft": "hold",
            "extendright": "hold"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "comp_over",
          "op_type": "overTOP",
          "params": {}
        }
      ],
      "connections": [
        {
          "out": "dens",
          "into": "tau_small"
        },
        {
          "out": "tau_small",
          "into": "tau_conv"
        },
        {
          "out": "tau_conv",
          "into": "tau_up"
        },
        {
          "out": "tau_up",
          "into": "trans_sigma"
        },
        {
          "out": "trans_sigma",
          "into": "trans"
        },
        {
          "out": "trans",
          "into": "scatter"
        },
        {
          "out": "dens",
          "into": "alpha_in"
        },
        {
          "out": "alpha_in",
          "into": "alpha_exp"
        },
        {
          "out": "alpha_exp",
          "into": "alpha_inv"
        },
        {
          "out": "scatter",
          "into": "smoke",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "alpha_inv",
          "into": "smoke",
          "in_index": 1
        },
        {
          "out": "smoke",
          "into": "smoke_pm"
        },
        {
          "out": "smoke_pm",
          "into": "comp_over",
          "in_index": 0
        },
        {
          "out": "bg",
          "into": "comp_over",
          "in_index": 1
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Optical depth as a convolution: the kernel is a line integral toward the light, so ONE operator replaces a raymarch. Compute it at 128x128 (optical depth is a smooth quantity) and bilinearly upsample. trans_sigma is a channelmix so the three extinction coefficients differ per channel: that alone gives cold shadows and warm highlights with no grading. scatter is albedo*light*T + ambient, again one channelmix. alpha = 1 - exp(-D*density).",
      "pitfalls": [
        "A kernel that is a ONE-PIXEL-WIDE line of taps produces a hard terminator and the result reads as cartoon cel-shading. Widen it into a cone (half-width growing with distance) and add ~20% isotropic weight to approximate multiple scattering.",
        "overTOP composites with PREMULTIPLIED alpha. With straight alpha the background is ignored and empty areas come out at the smoke colour, not the backdrop.",
        "The view extinction (alpha) must be consistent with the light extinction (sigma). With D=2.6 against sigma=15 the median alpha was 0.15 and the whole tonal range collapsed to near black over the backdrop.",
        "Normalising the kernel to sum 1 makes tau a weighted MEAN, not an integral \u2014 sigma must be scaled up accordingly (measured: 10x).",
        "rampTOP type='radial' has a seam at the half-height row (measured jump 0.044). Use vertical for backdrops.",
        "Shading the density with normalmapTOP + N.L above ~0.09 makes the smoke look like a wax surface instead of a volume."
      ],
      "references": [
        "Beer-Lambert law",
        "Harris 2003, Real-Time Cloud Rendering"
      ],
      "verified_on_build": "2025.32820"
    }
  ]
}